      "most_cognitive_tests_were_designed_for": " Most cognitive tests were designed for primates first, then adapted to other animals. Mirror tests, Y-mazes, tool-shaping puzzles — these all assume a centralized brain making centralized decisions. Cephalopod cognition keeps PARTIALLY passing tests it was never designed for. The honest interpretation: we don't yet have good tests for distributed-arm cognition or swarm intelligence. ",
      "most_common_jellyfish_in_temperate_sea": "Most common jellyfish in temperate seas. Their sting is too weak to seriously injure humans, but it irritates eyes + mucous membranes.",
      "most_cultures_don_t_question_eating_ce": "Most cultures don't question eating cephalopods — they're part of generations of cuisine. But the recent recognition of cephalopod sentience (UK 2021, EU 2010, multiple scientific declarations) has surfaced a question many find newly difficult:",
      "most_marine_biodiversity_hot_spots_are": "Most marine biodiversity hot spots are rocky substrates — they offer more crevice habitat per unit area than sand.",
