      "answer_a_wadati_benioff_zone_is_the_in": "Answer: A Wadati-Benioff zone is the inclined plane of earthquakes that marks a subducting slab. Earthquakes occur as the slab bends, cracks, and undergoes phase changes. Some Wadati-Benioff zones extend to 700 km depth.",
      "answer_a_wadati_benioff_zone_is_the_in_2": "Answer: A Wadati-Benioff zone is the inclined plane of earthquakes that marks a subducting slab. Earthquakes occur as the slab bends, cracks, and undergoes phase changes. Some Wadati-Benioff zones extend to 700 km depth.",
      "answer_a_wadati_benioff_zone_is_the_in_3": "Answer: A Wadati-Benioff zone is the inclined plane of earthquakes that marks a subducting slab. Earthquakes occur as the slab bends, cracks, and undergoes phase changes. Some Wadati-Benioff zones extend to 700 km depth.",
