      "standard_concerns_peer_review_is_slow_": "Standard concerns: peer review is slow (months to years), unevenly rigorous (different reviewers reach different conclusions), biased (toward established figures + Western institutions + native English-speakers), uncompensated (reviewers work free). Reform efforts include paid peer review (some journals), automated triage (using AI to identify obviously-flawed papers before human review), and registered reports (review the methodology BEFORE the experiment runs, then commit to publishing regardless of result).",
